[?2004hroot@1785664c22b0:/task# cat /task/input/acquisition_notes.md
[?2004l# Acquisition notes - experiment IMM-FC-012_PBMC_lineage (16-SEP-2025)

- Instrument: LSRFortessa X-20 (405/488/561/640 nm), FACSDiva 9.0, daily CS&T passed.
- Parameters recorded: FSC-A, FSC-H, SSC-A, eight fluorescence areas (see panel.tsv), Time. Detector voltages are stored in the files.
- Staining: surface antibody cocktail plus Zombie Aqua fixable viability dye, 1% PFA fixation. The reagent lots of the cocktail are listed in panel.tsv, the lot used for each control tube in controls.tsv.
- Material: cryopreserved PBMC, thawed on the day of staining; trypan blue viability after thaw between 80% and 92% depending on the donor.
- Tubes were vortexed briefly and run at medium flow rate (300-350 events/s) without straining through a filter cap.
- Experiment template: created on 26-MAY-2024, when the panel was first set up on this instrument; its compensation values date from that set-up. The detector voltages of the panel were re-optimised after the laser service of 04-JAN-2025. The compensation setup of the acquisition software was not run for this session; the experiment was recorded with the template compensation and exported as FCS 3.1 (the export stores the detector signals as recorded and the template values in the file header).
- Controls recorded at the start of the session with the panel voltages: one unstained PBMC tube; antibody-capture beads (positive and negative beads in the same tube) for the seven antibody conjugates, stained the day before from the vials that were open at the time; Zombie Aqua on a 1:1 mix of live and heat-killed PBMC; an aliquot of the reference pool stained with CD8 PerCP-Cy5.5 alone, taken from the vial that was used for the cocktail (ctrl_PerCPCy55_cells.fcs); the HLA-DR FMO tube (reference pool, complete cocktail without HLA-DR PE-Cy7).
- After PBMC_D829 the HLA-DR signal of the T cells was judged too close to the axis, and the voltage of YG780-A was raised from 641 V to 703 V. PBMC_D858 and all later tubes were recorded with the new voltage. Recorded again with the new voltage before continuing: the PE-Cy7 capture-bead tube (same tube, ctrl_PECy7_rerun.fcs) and the HLA-DR FMO tube (same tube, fmo_HLADR_rerun.fcs). No other control was recorded again.
- PBMC_D858: large events were piling up in the top FSC channel during the first attempt, so the tube was re-acquired after the FSC voltage had been lowered from 420 V to 348 V. Only the re-acquisition was exported. The fluorescence detectors were not touched for this.
